Q: How do we allocate a 2-D array using One malloc statement
A: <blockquote>
  <p>How do we allocate a 2-D array using One malloc statement (?)</p>
</blockquote>

<p>No answers, so far, allocate memory for a true 2D array.</p>

<p><code>int **array</code> is a <a href="https://cdecl.org/?q=int+**Array" rel="noreferrer">pointer to pointer to int</a>.  <code>array</code> is not a pointer to a 2D array.</p>

<p><code>int a[2][3]</code> is an example of a true 2D array or <a href="https://cdecl.org/?q=int+A%5B2%5D%5B3%5D" rel="noreferrer">array 2 of array 3 of int</a></p>

