<pre><code>var raceCursor = RacesCollection.find({eventId: "e1"});
var race;
while ( raceCursor.hasNext() ) {
    race = raceCursor.next();
    console.log( race.raceName );
}
</code></pre>

<p>Since Meteor is pure javascript, it also supports using <code>forEach()</code> to iterate over the cursor's documents, as in <a href="http://docs.meteor.com/#foreach" rel="noreferrer">this example</a>. </p>

