Q: Await inside finally block in an async function doesn't wait
A: <p>Node does not wait for any particular promise, it only cares about the event loop. And it does terminate early when there is an unhandled exception anywhere (including unhandled promise rejections). And that is exactly your problem: your code is already <code>reject()</code>ing the <code>run</code> promise <em>before</em> the <code>finally</code> block runs, before the promise returned by the <code>async</code> function (which you are ignoring) is settled. And since you have not caught the rejection of <code>run</code> (e.g. using <code>run.then(console.log, console.error)</code>), nodejs exits while the function is still running.</p>
<p>To fix this, avoid the <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/q/23803743/1048572?What-is-the-promise-construction-antipattern-and-how-to-avoid-it"><code>Promise</code> constructor antipattern</a> and use</p>
