Q: regular expression for finding 'href' value of a <a> link
A: <p>I'd recommend using an HTML parser over a regex, but still here's a regex that will create a capturing group over the value of the <code>href</code> attribute of each links. It will match whether double or single quotes are used.</p>

<pre><code>&lt;a\s+(?:[^&gt;]*?\s+)?href=(["'])(.*?)\1
</code></pre>

<p>You can view a full explanation of this regex at <a href="https://regex101.com/r/rMAHrE/1" rel="noreferrer">here</a>.</p>

