for (vp = vertices(g); vp.first != vp.second; ++vp.first) {
   std::cout &lt;&lt; index[*vp.first] &lt;&lt;  " ";
}
</code></pre>

<p>This is how the "quick tour" suggests we print out a list of the graph vertices.  However, a little study shows that a vertex is no more than an integer index, and the code can be greatly simplified to</p>

